Debug harness: PLaMo 3 op-level WebGPU vs CPU suite in test-backend-ops.

Adds a --sakutto-plamo3 flag to test-backend-ops that replaces the default
eval list with the shapes and types PLaMo 3 Translate 0.8B Q4_K_M actually
runs (Q4_K/Q6_K mul_mat at the qkv/out/up/down/output shapes for 1..128
tokens, F16 KQ/KQV mul_mat with GQA ratio 16, GET_ROWS, RMS_NORM and the
fused RMS_NORM+MUL+ADD, MUL/ADD broadcast, SWIGLU, NEOX ROPE with and
without YaRN, masked SOFT_MAX, FLASH_ATTN_EXT 128/128 with one KV head,
SET_ROWS F32->F16, CPY, CONT, SCALE), and prints one machine-readable line
per compared node (SAKUTTO_OPSTAT: NMSE over finite values, threshold,
max abs error, NaN/Inf counts on each backend) and per case
(SAKUTTO_OPRESULT: OK/FAIL/NOT_SUPPORTED). Used only by the debug-only GPU
harness page through wllama's testBackendOps(); see patch 0016.

--- a/llama.cpp/tests/test-backend-ops.cpp
